        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Somme</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">1 July – 18 November 1916 (141 days)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Both sides of the upper reaches of the river Somme in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The British Fourth Army under Sir Henry Rawlinson, with the Third Army and later the Reserve Army under Hubert Gough, and the French Sixth Army under Émile Fayolle, under the overall direction of Douglas Haig and Joseph Joffre, against the German Second Army under Fritz von Below; more than three million men fought in all</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> advanced about 10 km along most of the front, their largest gain since the Marne in 1914, but did not take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peronne">Péronne</a> or Bapaume; casualties on all sides exceeded one million, and the German army withdrew to the Hindenburg Line in March 1917.</span></div>
        </div>
